  "body": "## What Happens\n\nThe browser build of `main` does not compile. `bash web/build-app-wasm.sh` (the release job's `wasm` step) stops in `camcraft-ui`:\n\n```\nerror[E0308]: mismatched types\n    --> crates/ui/src/state.rs:3130:46\n     |\n3130 |         crate::model_link_watch::check(self, Instant::now());\n     |                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `std::time::Instant`, found `camcraft_app::clock::Instant`\nnote: function defined here\n    --> crates/ui/src/model_link_watch.rs:60:15\n```\n\n`model_link_watch.rs` (the link check of #2463, PR #2563) takes `std::time::Instant`. `State` passes `camcraft_app::clock::Instant`, which is `web_time::Instant` on wasm32 (#31).\n\n## Steps To Reproduce\n\n1. Check out `main` (seen at 409c0b5ab).\n2. Run `bash web/build-app-wasm.sh` with a clang that has the wasm32 target (macOS: Homebrew LLVM, `CC_wasm32_unknown_unknown` and `AR_wasm32_unknown_unknown` set as in `release.yml`).\n\n## What Should Happen\n\nThe browser build compiles. The link check reads the clock seam (`camcraft_app::clock::Instant`) like the rest of the UI.\n\n## Note\n\nPR checks do not build wasm32, so this shows at the next cut's `wasm` job.\n",
